IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P8-gate`

-- P8-art75b: Article 75b, commitments (inserted by the Omnibus, `▼M1 INSERTED`). LAYER 1.
-- Group General (from 2 August 2026). Only the amended text exists: the Article is new.
-- The consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect.

DECLARE `Art 75b act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 75b make the commitments binding on the operator by decision and declare that there are no further grounds for action`
    `Art 75b reopen the proceedings`
    `Art 75b reject the commitments in a reasoned decision when concluding the proceedings`

-- src:1221 | If, during proceedings under Article 75a(2), the operator concerned offers commitments to ensure compliance with the relevant provisions of this Regulation, the AI Office may, by decision, make those commitments binding on the operator concerned and declare that there are no further grounds for action. The AI Office may, upon request or on its own initiative, reopen the proceedings where:
@ref Art 75b first paragraph, first sentence (src:1221)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `during proceedings under Article 75a(2) the operator concerned offers commitments to ensure compliance with the relevant provisions of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75b first sentence the AI Office may make the commitments binding on the operator and declare that there are no further grounds for action` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `during proceedings under Article 75a(2) the operator concerned offers commitments to ensure compliance with the relevant provisions of this Regulation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power gated by "If": the grant ruling of 2026-11-12 gives NOTHING for a failed "if" gate of a power (fork F-75b-if)

-- src:1221 | If, during proceedings under Article 75a(2), the operator concerned offers commitments to ensure compliance with the relevant provisions of this Regulation, the AI Office may, by decision, make those commitments binding on the operator concerned and declare that there are no further grounds for action. The AI Office may, upon request or on its own initiative, reopen the proceedings where:
@ref Art 75b first paragraph, first sentence (src:1221)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `during proceedings under Article 75a(2) the operator concerned offers commitments to ensure compliance with the relevant provisions of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75b act`
`Art 75b first sentence the AI Office's choice to make the commitments binding on the operator` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `during proceedings under Article 75a(2) the operator concerned offers commitments to ensure compliance with the relevant provisions of this Regulation`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or the conditions of the duty are not met
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office`
        MAY `Art 75b make the commitments binding on the operator by decision and declare that there are no further grounds for action`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1221 | If, during proceedings under Article 75a(2), the operator concerned offers commitments to ensure compliance with the relevant provisions of this Regulation, the AI Office may, by decision, make those commitments binding on the operator concerned and declare that there are no further grounds for action. The AI Office may, upon request or on its own initiative, reopen the proceedings where:
-- src:1222 | (a) there has been a material change in any of the facts on which the decision was based;
-- src:1223 | (b) the operator acts contrary to its commitments; or
-- src:1224 | (c) the decision was based on incomplete, incorrect or misleading information provided by the operator concerned.
@ref Art 75b first paragraph, second sentence and points (a) to (c) (src:1221-1224)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `there has been a material change in any of the facts on which the decision was based` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the operator acts contrary to its commitments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision was based on incomplete, incorrect or misleading information provided by the operator concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75b second sentence the AI Office may reopen the proceedings` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF     `there has been a material change in any of the facts on which the decision was based`
             OR `the operator acts contrary to its commitments`
             OR `the decision was based on incomplete, incorrect or misleading information provided by the operator concerned`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The AI Office may, upon request or on its own initiative, reopen the proceedings where: (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..." (a "may" gated by "where": split site (ii), fork F-75b-where)

-- src:1221 | If, during proceedings under Article 75a(2), the operator concerned offers commitments to ensure compliance with the relevant provisions of this Regulation, the AI Office may, by decision, make those commitments binding on the operator concerned and declare that there are no further grounds for action. The AI Office may, upon request or on its own initiative, reopen the proceedings where:
-- src:1222 | (a) there has been a material change in any of the facts on which the decision was based;
-- src:1223 | (b) the operator acts contrary to its commitments; or
-- src:1224 | (c) the decision was based on incomplete, incorrect or misleading information provided by the operator concerned.
@ref Art 75b first paragraph, second sentence and points (a) to (c) (src:1221-1224)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `there has been a material change in any of the facts on which the decision was based` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the operator acts contrary to its commitments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision was based on incomplete, incorrect or misleading information provided by the operator concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75b act`
`Art 75b second sentence the AI Office's choice to reopen the proceedings` MEANS
    IF     (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`))
       OR ((NOT `there has been a material change in any of the facts on which the decision was based`) AND (NOT `the operator acts contrary to its commitments`) AND (NOT `the decision was based on incomplete, incorrect or misleading information provided by the operator concerned`))
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is permitted: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or none of the grounds of points (a) to (c) holds
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office`
        MAY `Art 75b reopen the proceedings`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1225 | Where the AI Office considers that the commitments offered by the operator concerned are unable to ensure effective compliance with the relevant provisions of this Regulation, it shall reject those commitments in a reasoned decision when concluding the proceedings.
@ref Art 75b second paragraph (src:1225)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office considers that the commitments offered by the operator concerned are unable to ensure effective compliance with the relevant provisions of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75b second paragraph the AI Office must reject the commitments in a reasoned decision when concluding the proceedings` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the AI Office considers that the commitments offered by the operator concerned are unable to ensure effective compliance with the relevant provisions of this Regulation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the AI Office considers that the commitments ... are unable to ensure effective compliance ..., it shall reject those commitments in a reasoned decision" (an unmet "where" gate counts as the text's no: ruling (b)) (fork F-75b-second-par-duty)

-- src:1225 | Where the AI Office considers that the commitments offered by the operator concerned are unable to ensure effective compliance with the relevant provisions of this Regulation, it shall reject those commitments in a reasoned decision when concluding the proceedings.
@ref Art 75b second paragraph (src:1225)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office considers that the commitments offered by the operator concerned are unable to ensure effective compliance with the relevant provisions of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 75b act`
`Art 75b second paragraph the AI Office's duty to reject the commitments in a reasoned decision` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the AI Office considers that the commitments offered by the operator concerned are unable to ensure effective compliance with the relevant provisions of this Regulation`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or the conditions of the duty are not met
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office`
        MUST `Art 75b reject the commitments in a reasoned decision when concluding the proceedings`
        HENCE FULFILLED
